  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.553,
            0.048,
            0.862,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Baudhāyana-Pythagoras Theorem"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.087,
            0.576,
            0.109
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_1.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{S}0,(\\sqrt{72})^{2}=2a^{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.489,
            0.118,
            0.578,
            0.138
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "7 2 = 2 a ^ { 2 } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.436,
            0.151,
            0.614,
            0.178
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Thus}, a^{2} = \\frac{72}{2} = 36."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.465,
            0.184,
            0.616,
            0.206
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{S}0, a = \\sqrt{36} = 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.21,
            0.649,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, each of the other two sides has length 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.229,
            0.839,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Use this formula to check your answers in the Figure it Out on page 39."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.273,
            0.668,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.4 Combining Two Different Squares"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.306,
            0.848,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen in the previous sections how to combine two copies of the same square to make a larger square whose area is the sum of the areas of the two smaller squares."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.376,
            0.807,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.376,
                0.807,
                0.514
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.532,
            0.847,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sidelength of the larger square is the length of the diagonal of either of the smaller squares."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.58,
            0.846,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What if we wish to combine two squares of ‘different’ sizes to make a large square whose area is the sum of the two smaller squares?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.634,
            0.732,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.192,
                0.634,
                0.732,
                0.774
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.793,
            0.847,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In his Śulba-Sūtra (Verse 1.12), Baudhāyana also gives a truly remarkable solution to this more general problem of combining two different sized squares. He writes:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.872,
            0.829,
            0.913
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The area of the square produced by the diagonal is the sum of the areas of the squares produced by the two sides."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.876,
            0.914,
            0.911,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "41"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
